Bruce, I'D LOVE YOUR FEEDBACK!

Thank you for being a student of Dispute 21, I hope you're enjoying the
content. I know we are just getting into the dispute process and you
still have a few more lessons + bonuses coming your way, but I'd greatly
appreciate your honest feedback of your experience with the content so
far. 

* Do you feel the course is worth the money you paid for it?

* Do you have a favorite lesson? Least favorite lesson?

* Are there other topics you would have liked me to cover in this
course?

* Were the lessons too long, short or just enough?

* Would you have preferred companion tools to assist with your learning:
videos, worksheets, a workbook, etc.?

* Are there any topics, products, courses that you would like to be made
available to grow your knowledge of credit and your understanding of the
dispute process?

Bruce, Day 17 was all about cleaning up personal information when
preparing a client's file for the dispute process. My team and I have
experienced GREAT Success in this area using online real time reports,
like those in the screen shots I showed you in the lesson, to pull all
of the client's personal information that we never see on the 3rd party
monitoring reports and the consumer disclosures (*aka*credit reports).
Bruce, I'm talking sometimes more than 30+ physical addresses and
name variations that we would have never known were reporting if we'd
never had access to those real time reports! Having access to this
information heightens your chance of successfully removing personal
information and disputing negative, erroneous, inaccurate and
unverifiable items on the credit report. 

Would You Like Access To This Information???

Yes? I got you! In exchange for your honest review of Dispute 21, I'll
send you the links to the bureaus online reports where you can get
information in it's most current form so that you can see updates before
they reach your client's mailbox, access the hidden personal information
that the reporting agencies don't want you to know they're reporting +
detailed instructions on how to properly dispute personal information
obtained from these reports to prevent address identification match up
used by the bureaus to easily verify negative accounts.

Please understand I'm not looking for smoke and mirror reviews to
deceive the public into purchasing products. This is not a leave me a 5
star review and I'll send you a gift type deal. EduCredit is a premier
credit education company and we only strive to deliver you high quality
up to date content in a manner that's understandable and easy to consume
so that you can learn and grow. Your feedback is very important. 

Leave a Review 
